The migration is not idempotent if the user already has one of these addons listed under `deviceAddons` (e.g. a partially migrated config): it will remove from `addons` and unconditionally append to `deviceAddons`, potentially creating duplicates. Consider checking existing `deviceAddons` entries (e.g. via `ConfigFile.getNamesFromPath(['deviceAddons'])`) and only appending when the addon isn’t already present.
```suggestion
      const existingDeviceAddonNames = new Set(main.getNamesFromPath(['deviceAddons']));

      for (const addon of ondeviceAddons) {
        const name = getAddonName(addon);
        main.removeEntryFromArray(['addons'], name);

        if (!existingDeviceAddonNames.has(name)) {
          main.appendValueToArray(['deviceAddons'], addon);
          existingDeviceAddonNames.add(name);
        }
